{"name":"Axolotl","hex":"#fff0df","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"axolotl","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A critically endangered salamander found in the elevated lakes of Mexico, Ambystoma mexicanum."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/axolotl"}],"entries":[{"title":"Axolotl","blocks":[{"text":"The axolotl is a species of mole salamander. It is neotenic, reaching sexual maturity without undergoing metamorphosis, and the adults remain fully aquatic with obvious external gills. Axolotls may be difficult to distinguish from the larval stage of other neotenic adult mole salamanders, in particular the tiger salamander, or other species such as mudpuppies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Axolotl_ganz.jpg/330px-Axolotl_ganz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axolotl","wikidata":"Q22718"},{"title":"Axolotl (short story)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Axolotl\" is a work of short fiction by Julio Cortázar, first appearing in the Spanish language collection Final del juego (1956), and first in the English language in End of the Game and Other Stories (1963)."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axolotl_(short_story)","wikidata":"Q137441667"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Axolot%27s_head_%28Ambystoma_mexicanum%29.jpg/500px-Axolot%27s_head_%28Ambystoma_mexicanum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Axolot%27s_head_%28Ambystoma_mexicanum%29.jpg/1280px-Axolot%27s_head_%28Ambystoma_mexicanum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Axolot%27s_head_%28Ambystoma_mexicanum%29.jpg/500px-Axolot%27s_head_%28Ambystoma_mexicanum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pars